{
  "name": "What to consider before drywalling your garage?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about drywalling your garage? Awesome! It’s a great way to upgrade the space, but there are a few things you should really think about first to make sure it’s done right. First, you'll want to check for any moisture issues or leaks. You don't want to trap moisture behind new drywall! Then, you've got to decide on the right thickness and type of drywall. For walls shared with your living space, you're usually looking at a minimum of 1/2-inch drywall, and if there’s a living space above your garage, 5/8-inch fire-resistant Type X is often required by code. Don't forget about staggering those seams and keeping the drywall slightly off the floor to prevent moisture wicking. It’s also super important to make sure your quote includes not just hanging, but also the taping, mudding, and finishing. If fire rating, tricky ceiling heights, or local permit questions come into play, that’s when a qualified pro like HH Remodeling LLC, serving the entire Denver metro area, really becomes essential. We’re happy to answer your questions and provide a clear plan. Just give us a ring at 303-505-0866!",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
